{"author":{"id":"d28e897521accad965e5a3acfc75f906eaa0157f711e26b2841e79fd25d0ef35"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788468165,"nonce":"6xe1Ana4IAU+Aj0oRVIh2+a2EnE=","title":"Add OpenRadiation radiation unit","message":"Panel radiation unit (µSv/h → Civilization dose-rate unit) is blocked on two things:\n\n1. Hardware: acquire a Geiger counter compatible with OpenRadiation's app so we can start submitting readings at this Lokit and building up local coverage. OpenRadiation is crowdsourced and has zero coverage near Absecon -- old data is better than none.\n\n2. API key: request a key from dev@openradiation.net (the test key bde8ebc61cb089b8cc997dd7a0d0a434 is available for development).\n\nOnce local coverage exists, the pull side is straightforward:\n- Endpoint: GET https://request.openradiation.net/measurements\n- Location filter: bounding box via minLatitude/maxLatitude/minLongitude/maxLongitude\n- Auth: apiKey query param\n- Response: JSON, measurements in µSv/h\n- No auth needed to explore; key needed for production pulls\n\nUnit question is also open: musa.bet may define a dose-rate unit distinct from Sychnit (which is activity, not dose rate). Needs research before the conversion factor can be written.","files":null}]}